  - id: author.tool.iron_headed_digger
    name: Iron-headed multi-tool
    purpose: 'A full-length, two-handed iron-headed multi-tool with a transverse
      dual-ended head: a broad downturned hoe/adze-like digging blade on one side
      and a rough blunt iron hammer poll on the other. Its stone-bone shaft, reinforcing
      iron collar, shell butt cap, iron retaining pin and captured gripping-pad scales
      make a more effective prying and shallow-digging tool than the bone version.'
    category: Tools
    tier: T1
    rarity: Common
    artName: iron-headed-multi-tool-completion-v4
    sourceStatus: catalog revision 154
    equipmentAddress: tool
    inputs:
    - itemId: component.mining.iron_digging_head
      quantity: 1
    - itemId: component.mining.bone_shaft
      quantity: 1
    - itemId: component.mining.shell_butt_cap
      quantity: 1
    - itemId: component.mining.iron_head_collar
      quantity: 1
    - itemId: component.mining.iron_retaining_pin
      quantity: 1
