  stations:
  - id: author.station.workbench
    name: Workbench
    purpose: General camp work surface for fitting parts, assembling tools and repairing
      ordinary gear. The existing Camp Loop trial uses its workbench to craft an
      empty Arc Battery; this catalog entry does not expand the trial recipe roster.
  - id: author.station.dust_refinery
    name: Dust refinery
    purpose: Refine collected Arc Dust into Arc Energy and charge an existing empty
      Arc Battery. Accept a dust canister and an empty battery, retain the canister
      and unused dust, and return the same battery charged; dust alone does not create
      a battery casing.
  - id: author.station.ironstone_refinery
    name: Ironstone refinery
    purpose: Camp facility for breaking down and separating raw Ironstone Ore into
      coarse aggregate, iron-rich concentrate, mineral sand and mineral dust. Represents
      the existing manual Ironstone sorter; further refining or smelting would require
      separately designed operations.
  - id: camp-menu.cooking
    name: Cooking station
    purpose: Prepare food at camp. Ingredients, preparation, heat and atmosphere
      requirements are still to be designed.
  - id: proposal.station.ceramic_forming_bench
    name: Ceramic forming bench
    purpose: Prepare and shape qualified ceramic feed into unfired vessels, molds
      or fitted blanks before drying and kiln firing. Complements the existing firing
      kiln; binder chemistry, usable process liquids and feed suitability must be
      selected explicitly.
  - id: proposal.station.contained_chemical_processing_station
    name: Contained chemical processing station
    purpose: Process separately contained faunal and mineral feedstocks into candidate
      industrial binders, sealants, lubricants or other processing agents. Select
      compatible vessels and a qualified process for each product; keep industrial
      chemicals separate from Phagia and food equipment.
  - id: proposal.audit.controlled_heating_firing_kiln
    name: Controlled-heating firing kiln
    purpose: Candidate stationary kiln. Qualified external power, thermal controls
      and atmosphere management remain unresolved.
  - id: proposal.forging.hearth
    name: Forge hearth
    purpose: Proposed bounded workshop heat source for bringing metal to a workable
      state. It supports a controlled metalworking operation; the workpiece, heat
      source and suitable supporting tools must be established for the process.
  - id: proposal.station.husk_processing_table
    name: Husk processing table
    purpose: Hold shell husks and shed plates for scraping chitin/icore fibers and
      sorting useful shell pieces. Supplies candidate fiber feed for husk paper and
      later pressing; cheap raw shell does not imply cheap finished textiles.
  - id: proposal.station.husk_fiber_press
    name: Husk-fiber press
    purpose: Press prepared husk-fiber feed into candidate paper sheets or difficult
      dense fiber stock using process-specific tooling. Paper and garment-grade material
      remain separate processes; pressing alone does not supply ordinary cloth or
      bypass costly textile preparation.
  - id: proposal.station.legger_service_stand
    name: Legger service stand
    purpose: Support accessible Legger assemblies during inspection, cleaning, lubrication
      and replacement of compatible mechanical parts. Requires the Legger's physical
      presence and appropriate tools; service outcomes depend on parts and access
      rather than automatic full repair.
  - id: proposal.station.salvage_dismantling_bench
    name: Salvage dismantling bench
    purpose: Secure recovered scrap and damaged mechanisms for inspection and careful
      disassembly. Candidate outputs are sorted scrap and individually qualified
      reusable parts; dismantling does not guarantee repair or reproduce ancient
      technology.
  itemCatalog: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ce27add218970c14c9f30c664d1c0626, type: 2}
